    "https://jobs.mdx.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=ESE34-R3": {
      "title": "Alumni Communications and Engagement Assistant",
      "description": "ESE34-R3 Alumni Communications and Engagement Assistant - Careers at Middlesex University Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register Careers at MDX Careers at Middlesex Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ Alumni Communications and Engagement Assistant Job Details: Job Description Careers & Futures are looking for an Alumni Communications and Engagement Assistant to join our new Alumni team. The role will have a focus on Graduate Outcomes, providing data and communications to recent graduates, early years alumni and established alum. We are ideally looking for a recent graduate, interested in data collection, communications and outreach. The ideal candidate should have an understanding of the Middlesex 2031 strategy where we focus on building a partnership with our alumni. We would like the candidate to be someone who feels a strong sense of belonging to Middlesex, and is able to encourage our finalists to maintain a relationship both within the local community and Middlesex after they finish their studies. If you wish to discuss the job in further detail please contact Claire Yates Wedge, Careers and Employability Service Manager, by email on c.yates@mdx.ac.uk Middlesex is committed to fostering an inclusive working environment. We encourage applications from underrepresented groups including people from Black, Asian and minority ethnic groups, disabled people, LGBTQ+ people, women, and gender non-conforming individuals. All recruitment decisions will be based on merit. Email details to a friend Apply Online We value diversity and strive to create a fairer, more equitable work environment for our staff and students. We offer a range of family friendly, inclusive employment policies, flexible working arrangements, staff diversity networks, campus facilities and services to support staff from different backgrounds. Middlesex is home to a diverse community of professionals. We are a bronze award holder of the Athena Swan Charter and the Race Equality Charter, a Stonewall Top 100 employer and Gold award holder in 2023, and a Disability Confident Leader. Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Faculty/Executive Education & Student Experience Company MU Services Ltd Location Hendon Starting Salary £29,417\r\n            per annum Grade Grade 4 Contract Type Fixed Term - 18 months Hours per Week 35.5 Date Posted Wednesday 07 October 2026 Closing Date Tuesday 20 October 2026 Interview Date To be confirmed Reference ESE34-R3 Apply Online Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs Search Advanced Job Search Useful Links Careers at Middlesex About Us MU Services Limited Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility"
